      "groupIds": [
        "v_Mf8kyQ_Un3q5W7ovGdJ"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1Z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1404949699,
      "version": 282,
      "versionNonce": 42047395,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791468907102,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Good Old Days, BM25",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Good Old Days, BM25",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "created": 1791468518128,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29bMQi-I3i2icCClXNDIK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2369.667088499238,
      "y": 650.1811920897871,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 875,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "iT7U9D_aNunHv-ssHQ-go",
        "r81KaXKR72nhtpaX5YWGX",
        "P_-DNvb9UUGgDgFDTPrNo",
        "S3JNFc9YbCRmzoNB9L1cq",
        "Cwpbn7i_tC_3jI9Fm2OSS",
        "KEXUEK4nErUbissxvbMjz",
        "v_Mf8kyQ_Un3q5W7ovGdJ"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1a",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 256656483,
      "version": 8291,
      "versionNonce": 2052369219,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791468907102,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In the vector space model of information retrieval a document is represented as a vector of counts of\nthe words it contains. We sometimes call this kind of model a bag-of-words model,  an unordered set of\nwords with their position ignored, keeping only their frequency in the document.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMore generally, we can represent a set of documents as a term-document matrix in which each row\nrepresents a word in the vocabulary and each column represents a document from some collection of\ndocuments. Each cell in this matrix represents the number of times a particular word (defined by the\nrow) occurs in a particular document (defined by the column). \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTwo documents that are similar will tend to have similar words, and if two documents have similar words\ntheir column vectors will tend to be similar.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In the vector space model of information retrieval a document is represented as a vector of counts of the words it contains. We sometimes call this kind of model a bag-of-words model,  an unordered set of words with their position ignored, keeping only their frequency in the document.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMore generally, we can represent a set of documents as a term-document matrix in which each row represents a word in the vocabulary and each column represents a document from some collection of documents. Each cell in this matrix represents the number of times a particular word (defined by the row) occurs in a particular document (defined by the column). \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTwo documents that are similar will tend to have similar words, and if two documents have similar words their column vectors will tend to be similar.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1791468543597,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
